WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.887
A ticket closed with 'done'
is just an assertion.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:07.017
The book wants three records that
agree: the ticket shows the decision,

3
00:00:07.017 --> 00:00:11.501
the elevation record shows the privilege,
and the audit log shows the change.

4
00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:15.438
Two gaps have to be built, because
Entra won't close them for you.

5
00:00:15.438 --> 00:00:19.960
Privileged Identity Management asks for
a ticket number but never checks it,

6
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.776
so a detection rule has to match
every activation to a real ticket.

7
00:00:23.776 --> 00:00:28.025
And Entra keeps its logs for only
thirty days, so they go to the SIEM.

8
00:00:28.025 --> 00:00:31.290
The service levels on the
right are program defaults,

9
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.738
and a shorter outside clock always wins.

10
00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:37.060
Module 2 turns to the
roles behind all this.
